{
  "case_id": "2021-21a244",
  "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Scott A. Keller",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "OSHA's economy-wide one-size-fits-all mandate covering 84 million Americans is not a necessary, indispensable use of OSHA's extraordinary emergency power which this Court has recognized is narrowly circumscribed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's one of your main -- that -- that's one of your main objections, that this is not a workplace issue, it's -- it's an out-in-the-world issue, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Keller, I just want to make sure I understand what we should focus on here. Is the question whether this ETS is necessary to"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "protect the health of the general public, or is it whether it is necessary to protect just employees and not even all employees but only unvaccinated employees, people who have chosen independently not to be vaccinated and do not want to be vaccinated? Is that the proper focus?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to be importing into \"necessary\" a concept of strict scrutiny. Am I correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what's the difference between this and telling employers, where sparks are flying in the workplace, your workers have to be -- wear a mask?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "your very last sentence, you said the question is, who decides? And I think that that's right. I think that that is the question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What -- what should we look at?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose it is major enough, so accept that position for the sake of this question. Suppose the statutory language is general, broad, but doesn't speak specifically to the issue in question, but it is general and broad language. How do we sort out -- so you don't necessarily say the language is ambiguous. But it also doesn't speak specifically to the issue. How do -- how would you suggest we sort out that kind of question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So you're saying, Mr. Flowers, that the first step in OSHA's regulation is to identify the workforce, the problem in that workforce, and then regulate that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Flowers",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, in terms of what we mean by \"work-related danger,\" I think one way to think about that is, has the employer done or failed to do something that creates a risk the employee faces?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So this kind of goes to Justice Barrett's question, I believe, that if they were to focus on a risk arising out of a --a particular aspect of the workplace that creates a -- a risk of a different nature, like being packed closely together in a meat-packing plant, that could fairly be described as a work-related danger."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well -- well, why -- why not? I mean, this is a -- the combination of lots of people all going in to one indoor space and having to deal with each other for eight hours, 10 hours, however many hours a day, in those settings, the combination of the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Flowers",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLOWERS: We are seeking an immediate -- thanks for the question. We are seeking an immediate stay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Commitment Foundation",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0002-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Sotomayor suggests and as the amicus brief from the American Commitment Foundation shows, vaccines do not appear to be very effective in stopping the spread or transmission."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I want to come back to the question I asked Mr. Keller in light of all that's been said this morning so far about public health, about the value of vaccine to -- vaccines to the general public, because I want to make sure I understand precisely what the question is before us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You said: Well, you know, we understand that 18- to 29-year-olds, even though they're not going to die or wind up with very serious injuries, that they can spread. You don't -- you don't doubt that, that those people spread to other people who might be more vulnerable? You don't doubt that, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Flowers, I'd like to return to the question of -- of who decides."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "OSHA amassed substantial evidence of wide-sprayed -- widespread workplace outbreaks across all industries. It studied the science of how this virus is transmitted and found that workers are exposed to danger when they're inside together for as little as 15 minutes, and OSHA considered the extensive evidence that unvaccinated employees are at heightened risk of contracting the virus, of transmitting it to others and infecting their coworkers, and of suffering the gravest consequences, hospitalization and even death."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can I ask you a question --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 93,
        "start": 93
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But you mean \"brief,\" don't you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Agency",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the agency has announced that for employers who are acting in good faith, it is not going to enforce any of the provisions of this ETS until January 10."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Agency",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0004-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 99,
        "start": 99
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "COVID-19 is a grave danger, it's a physically harmful agent, and the agency found that these measures are essential to protect workers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Agency",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0004-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 102,
        "start": 102
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "OSHA commonly issues nationwide standards that govern all employers throughout the nation with respect to risks that exist throughout the nation, and that describes COVID-19."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 108,
        "start": 108
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Can I just say, General, that regulators think of risk/risk tradeoffs constantly when they make regulations, that there are constant situations in which there are risk/risk tradeoffs, risks on both sides, but one risk vastly outweighs another risk and that that comes up throughout regulatory space."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0005-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 113,
        "start": 113
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So, really, the question is between masking and testing and/or vaccine, but no employer is being put at risk greater than they choose to undertake themselves, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0006-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 130,
        "start": 130
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: General Prelogar, I have two questions, both of which address the status of this rule as an emergency temporary"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Scott A. Keller (Applicants)",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53aeb924bcde3513081a06427fe9e3459306e1498fa94da1df1827f0d4ebc7e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53aeb924bcde-0006-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 138,
        "start": 138
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF SCOTT A. KELLER ON BEHALF OF THE APPLICANTS IN NO. 21A244 MR. KELLER: Two points, Mr. Chief Justice. First, we need a stay now before enforcement starts. Our members have to submit publicly their plans to how to comply with this regulatory behemoth on Monday. Vaccines would need to occur by February 9. You would need two vaccines to comply. Those vaccines would have to start immediately. Tracking and recordkeeping cannot happen overnight."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
